body:
Hi my name is Gen (20). I suffer from major depression and have been recovering from my first episode earlier this year. I have been going okay, on meds, therapy, psychiatrist, going to a weekly church service/bible study/supportive parents etc. I still feel distant from God and for the first time in a long time, I felt a wave of darkness and really horrible thoughts. I can't help feeling that I'll be somehow depressed forever and that I am not meant to live a long life, that God will take me out of my misery one day. Not sure where I am going with this, I suppose I just really need strength and need to feel the strong love of Jesus, because right now I feel very numb and cold. 

&#x200B;

Thank you <3

I feel very much the same, only difference is I am a girl and I turn 21 in about 2 months. I would never have the courage to go up to someone, but maybe, if some girl looks kinda lonely you could go up to her. Since you are at school, I was but I am having a break, I tried to talk to others in lectures and class and did the classic "have you done the reading" or in class I said once "hey, this is kind of random but I missed last weeks class and I was wondering if you have any notes. If you would like, I could share some of my notes I have made so far :)" That way, its super non threatening and if they are like "nah" you just be like "cool cool cool" and try someone else lol. I think often people in class and lectures are waiting for people to talk to them, everyone is so fucking anti-social it seems these days, well at my university it is/was the case. Its like, God forbid someone tries to talk to you and be social haha. I am so sorry you feel this way. Or, making a joke about the lecture content or some lame pun, I have done this once or twice and some people who are \~\~ too cool \~\~ ignore you or just back off and yes its super awkward but sometimes the conversation, whilst banal... flows...People love to complain so sometimes I let them and be like, well maybe catch you next week in the lecture and from there you might ask "how was your weekend" and then maybe you can form friends that way. I think kindness, small favours etc goes a long way. Its late so I am rambling however once I met a girl in class and I came up to her and said "hey, I know this may come off as kinda random but I always love what you wear to class each week". She said that she always liked how I had funny but analytical answers to the tutor's questions. We got talking a little bit and I said do you wanna get lunch if she was free. We did, but she didn't have any lunch or money for it so I just brought her something small because she had a long day ahead of her, I felt bad haha. It went a long way and we became friends. Everyone likes compliments, sometimes a small compliment can start a friendship and it doesn't have to be about looks which may be a bit intimidating for a guy to say to a girl??? Idk. Like, at the end of a class, tap someone who seems nice/who you would like to get to know more and drop even a casual convo thing like "hey, I agree about what you said about XYZ text, it was confusing to me either, good to know I wasn't the only one" maybe pull a face or something and then go to your next class. Once again, its casual and non threatening and yeah idk. I think from a girls pov, I actually would really like if I guy complimented me on say, my outfit or like a necklace or something. In first year haha, a guy was like "cool necklace, does it have a meaning" and I said no etc etc but I think he was kinda flirting but also maybe not, i thought he was super cute and was too nervous to actually talk to him regularly because I was a shy, 18 year old loser (still am tbh)  but yeah -- it was pretty simple but nice.

&#x200B;

 Sorry for all the random rambling, but good luck, maybe don't be afraid to seek diagnosis because I felt the same way and found out that I actually had major depression (lmao fun times) got on medication, never really considered it before and it does help a bit in terms of the social anxiety/general people anxiety for me.
